ks with, and a server with a reachable port, two 2 GHz x86-64 CPU cores, 8 GB of RAM, 4 GB of swap and 20 GB free. No GPU is required. For a nonblank post, the reference miner calls OpenAI with an API key at an unstated price, but if it has no key, it returns one random crypto tag. If the text is blank, it returns no tags.","Validators give equal weight to agreement with other miners, relevance and label quality. Only the best tag per qualifying group counts, and the code divides by three even if fewer tags arrive. If 50 miners submit the same set, each keeps half its score. Observed miners share weight in proportion to the exponential of ten times their 24-hour average, so missing observations count as zeros and higher averages earn larger shares. The burn share is zero.","The cited settings give no registration protection period. Read from https://github.com/tag101-ai/tag101 at commit c3d788b on 2026-11-23."],"how_it_was_made":"This note was put together by AI agents and not by a person who mines here. One agent read the subnet's public repository and wrote down what a miner does, what it takes and how the work is paid, with a source for each statement, and a second agent opened every source and took out whatever it did not support. Of 24 source checks, 22 held, 2 did not hold and 0 could not be opened, and only what held is in the text above. Nothing of the subnet's code was run, and the note describes the code as it stood on the day and at the commit named in its last sentence, so it can be out of date.","page":"https://check.loopholetape.com/mine/101.html"},"read_until":"2026-11-25T12:05:36Z","weeks":[{"entered_from":"2026-10-26","entered_to":"2026-10-28","entries":124,"wallets":33,"typical_fee_usd":5.03,"earning_after_7_days":5,"counted_at_7_days":124,"earning_after_14_days":1,"counted_at_14_days":124,"got_fee_back":75,"counted_for_fee_back":124,"typical_result_usd":1.02},{"entered_from":"2026-10-28","entered_to":"2026-11-04","entries":416,"wallets":42,"typica